<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Shotpile: third-party licences</title>
<style>
  body { font: 14px/1.5 "Segoe UI", system-ui, sans-serif; max-width: 860px; margin: 32px auto; padding: 0 16px; color: #0a0e15; }
  pre { white-space: pre-wrap; background: #f7f8fb; border: 1px solid #e0e4ea; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px; font-size: 12px; }
  li { margin: 2px 0; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>Third-party licences</h1>
<p>Shotpile itself is under the PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0. It is built with the open-source
components below, which keep their own licences. Each licence text is listed once, with every component that uses it.</p>
<h2>Overview</h2>
<ul>
{{#each overview}}<li>{{name}}: {{count}} component(s)</li>
{{/each}}
</ul>
{{#each licenses}}
<h2 id="{{id}}">{{name}}</h2>
<p>Used by:</p>
<ul>
{{#each used_by}}<li>{{crate.name}} {{crate.version}}</li>
{{/each}}
</ul>
<pre>{{text}}</pre>
{{/each}}
<h2>Not from crates.io</h2>
<p>SQLite is compiled into the app through rusqlite and is in the public domain. Microsoft Edge WebView2 is part of Windows
and is not distributed with Shotpile.</p>
</body>
</html>
